(4584651, 655312, 91068, '<td valign="top">Thank you to everyone for the helpfull comments and the generous votes. I feel as my first post i did better than anticipated.<br/> <br/>To answer several PM''s and a few comments, this cup was not placed on the ground, i found it lying there on the walk to the train from work. It felt almost right to take a shot of it.</td>', 'Thank you to everyone for the helpfull comments and the generous votes. I feel as my first post i did better than anticipated. To answer several PM''s and a few comments, this cup was not placed on the ground, i found it lying there on the walk to the train from work. It felt almost right to take a shot of it.', '2008-03-25 00:36:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4584756, 656423, 26001, '<td valign="top">The only reason I did not vote for this image was...i found the can very "neat and clean". which made it a promo shot instead of a pollution/litter shot for me. then again, i wasn''t convinced completely about that feeling either, so did not vote :)</td>', 'The only reason I did not vote for this image was...i found the can very "neat and clean". which made it a promo shot instead of a pollution/litter shot for me. then again, i wasn''t convinced completely about that feeling either, so did not vote :)', '2008-03-25 03:16:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4586531, 656496, 32933, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kmtregoe:</b></div><hr/><i> cropping the right side of the page would have created a stronger image </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yeah, I think I was just being stupid while editing. I love how the smoke turned out in the photo, so I really didn''t want to crop out any of the smoke, whatsoever. Like I said, I was being stupid and stubborn.</td>', 'Originally posted by kmtregoe: cropping the right side of the page would have created a stronger image   Yeah, I think I was just being stupid while editing. I love how the smoke turned out in the photo, so I really didn''t want to crop out any of the smoke, whatsoever. Like I said, I was being stupid and stubborn.', '2008-03-25 19:01:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4587090, 655385, 67697, '<td valign="top">This is a good interpretation of the theme.  I bet recycling is incredibly important in Japan.  Interesting to see this stuff sorted instead of just tossed in a pile.</td>', 'This is a good interpretation of the theme.  I bet recycling is incredibly important in Japan.  Interesting to see this stuff sorted instead of just tossed in a pile.', '2008-03-25 23:21:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4587118, 656862, 32933, '<td valign="top">This meets the challenge for me because of a study I did a few years ago on light pollution, for a middle school science fair, admittedly, but a study nonetheless. Astronomers should be pretty familiar with the term. When you''re traveling on the Interstate at night, and you see a sort of haze in the direction of a reasonably-sized city, you''re seeing the effects of light pollution. :)</td>', 'This meets the challenge for me because of a study I did a few years ago on light pollution, for a middle school science fair, admittedly, but a study nonetheless. Astronomers should be pretty familiar with the term. When you''re traveling on the Interstate at night, and you see a sort of haze in the direction of a reasonably-sized city, you''re seeing the effects of light pollution. :)', '2008-03-25 23:32:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4587454, 656295, 31637, '<td valign="top">you needed to see the specific pollutants , and this would have made top 3 for sure.</td>', 'you needed to see the specific pollutants , and this would have made top 3 for sure.', '2008-03-26 01:21:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4587618, 656901, 87609, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by emerygirl25:</b></div><hr/><i> You can''t really tell if this is just a tidal wave, but nice idea. This is a beautiful picture though. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Actually this is the waste chemical water discarded from Oil drilling rigs...due to water currants it made a long  white line...</td>', 'Originally posted by emerygirl25: You can''t really tell if this is just a tidal wave, but nice idea. This is a beautiful picture though.  Actually this is the waste chemical water discarded from Oil drilling rigs...due to water currants it made a long  white line...', '2008-03-26 04:39:30.000000', NULL, 0),
